<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Khana Ratsadon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1927">1927</a>–<a href="/years/1933">1933</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as People's Party (Siam)</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Khana Ratsadon, or People's Party, was a group of civilian and military officials founded by Thai students in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> in 1927. Led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pridi-banomyong">Pridi Banomyong</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/plaek-phibunsongkhram">Plaek Phibunsongkhram</a>, it carried out the bloodless revolution of 24 June 1932 that ended <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/absolute-monarchy">absolute monarchy</a> under King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prajadhipok">Prajadhipok</a> and introduced Siam's first constitution. Its members dominated Thai politics for the next fifteen years.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/khana-ratsadon.jpg" alt="Khana Ratsadon" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jo Shigeru · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Memorial_peg_of_Siamese_Revolution_of_2475.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>On 24 June 1932 the <b>People’s Party</b> (Khana Ratsadon), a small group of civilian and military officials led by Phraya Phahon Phonphayuhasena, Pridi Banomyong and Plaek Phibunsongkhram, seized key points in Bangkok in a bloodless coup, detained leading princes and demanded a constitutional regime.</blockquote><a href="/empire/rattanakosin-kingdom">Rattanakosin Kingdom · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>About five days after the coup of June 1932, Luang Nithetkolakit revealed that he was a member of the People's Party (<b>Khana Ratsadon</b>) and asked again, now on behalf of the new regime.</blockquote><a href="/songs/thai-national-anthem">Thai National Anthem</a></li><li><blockquote>The revolution of 24 June 1932 by the <b>Khana Ratsadon</b>, led by Pridi Banomyong and Plaek Phibunsongkhram, ended absolute monarchy in the Rattanakosin Kingdom and introduced a constitution.</blockquote><a href="/state/thailand">Thailand</a></li></ul></section>
